{"id": "long-buried-question", "category": "long_query", "difficulty": "medium", "expected_mode": "quick", "query": "So I've been planning a trekking trip to Nepal for about two years now, mostly reading forums and watching vlogs, and my friends keep arguing about whether you can cook rice properly at Everest Base Camp because of the altitude, and one of them insists that water boils at exactly 100 degrees everywhere because that's what we learned in school, while another says it's way lower up there, and honestly I just want to settle this before we leave in March. At what temperature does water boil at the summit of Mount Everest?", "assertions": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "\\b(6[89]|7[01])(\\.\\d)?\\s*°?\\s*C"}], "rubric": ["Answers the boiling point at the summit (about 68-71 °C)", "Explains it is lower because of lower air pressure", "Stays focused on the question instead of planning the whole trip"], "notes": "long preamble, simple question: tests that length alone does not trigger deep research"}
